---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { loadEntries, stats as fromData } from '../lib/entries.js';

const s = fromData(loadEntries());
---
<Base title="About" description="What a howff is, and why Grok Bots need one." path="/about">
  <main id="main" class="page">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>A place you go.</h1>
      <p>
        Howff is a Scots word for a haunt. A meeting-place. The pub you keep going back to.
        This one is for Grok Bots.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">Pronounced HOWFF · how + f. Not an acronym.</p>

      <h2>The gap</h2>
      <p>
        A Grok Bot is shared as a link. You click it, you trust it, and you have no idea what
        it was told to do. The prompt is the whole product, and it is the one part you cannot
        see. Links rot, nobody can diff them, and a bot only improves if its author happens
        to come back to it.
      </p>
      <p>
        So: put the instructions in a git repo. Every bot on this shelf carries its full prompt
        as a markdown file you can read before you add it, copy into your own chat, or improve
        by opening a pull request. {s.withInstructions} of {s.total} bots here do. The rest are
        native share links whose prompts are not public anywhere, and their pages say so
        plainly rather than pretending otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>
        The repo is the CMS. One <code>&lt;slug&gt;.json</code> for the metadata and one
        <code>&lt;slug&gt;.md</code> for the instructions, both in <code>data/entries/</code>.
        A script validates every file in CI. The site is static HTML with no backend, no
        accounts, and no tracking. MIT. See <a href="/contribute">contribute</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Credit where it is due</h2>
      <p>Most of this shelf came from two people who did the work first:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/mergisi/awesome-grokbot">mergisi/awesome-grokbot</a>
          · CC0-1.0 · the bulk of the catalogue.
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://github.com/HAEGONG/grok-bot-profiles">HAEGONG/grok-bot-profiles</a>
          · CC-BY-4.0 · the development bots. Attribution is a licence condition, so every
          page carries it.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Grok and Grok Bot are xAI products. Howff is not affiliated with xAI. Official docs:
        <a href="https://docs.x.ai/grok-bot/bots">docs.x.ai/grok-bot/bots</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>The shelf, counted</h2>
      <table class="stat-table">
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Bots</td><td class="num">{s.total}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>With full instructions</td><td class="num">{s.withInstructions}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>One-click share links</td><td class="num">{s.byAdd['share-link']}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Checked by a maintainer</td><td class="num">{s.verified}</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Integrations covered</td><td class="num">{s.integrations.length}</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="muted">
        Counted from <code>data/entries/</code> at build time. No invented analytics.
      </p>
      <p>
        Kept by Nikola Babic · org howffdotdev ·
        <a href="https://github.com/howffdotdev/howff">source on GitHub</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
